    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "NORTH'S PROPERTY presents Apt 14, 6 Ushers Quay, a well-presented first-floor one-bedroom apartment situated within this mature and well-established residential development. \nExtending to approximately 40 sq. m. (430 sq. ft.), the apartment offers well-proportioned accommodation comprising an entrance hallway, spacious open-plan living/ kitchen area, generous double bedroom, bathroom, hotpress and additional storage.\nThe bright and welcoming living/kitchen area is positioned to the rear of the apartment and benefits from large windows, excellent natural light and private balcony away from the hustle and bustle of cthe city. The light-coloured décor and wood-effect laminate flooring further enhance the sense of space and brightness.\nThe spacious double bedroom has fitted wardrobes provide excellent storage while maximising the available floor space. \nThe bathroom is fully tiled and features contrasting wall and floor tiling, with an electric shower.\nA hotpress and separate storage area are conveniently located off the entrance hallway. Heating throughout the apartment is electric, with updated heaters fitted, while the windows are PVC double glazed.\nThe development benefits from secure entrance doors and gates, with intercom systems serving the entrance and common areas.\nManagement Company Fee: ?1,340 per annum (2025)\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER C3\nBER No. 11331757\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Directions",
        "SortOrder": 5,
        "Content": "Ideally located at 6 Ushers Quay, Dublin 8, this apartment offers a convenient city-centre setting close to Smithfield, Stoneybatter, the Liberties and Dublin's main retail and business districts.\nA wide range of cafés, restaurants, bars, shops and cultural attractions are within walking distance, including Smithfield Square, Lighthouse Cinema, Stoneybatter and the Liberties. Phoenix Park is approximately a 15-minute walk away.\nTransport links are excellent, with the Four Courts LUAS stop just 300 metres away, providing easy access to the city centre, Docklands, IFSC and Connolly Station. Heuston Station is also just two LUAS stops away, with numerous bus routes and cycle lanes nearby.\nThe property is conveniently located for Trinity College Dublin, the Royal College of Surgeons and TU Dublin Grangegorman.\nWith attractive River Liffey views, generous accommodation and potential for modernisation, this is an excellent opportunity to acquire a well-located city-centre apartment.\nViewing is strictly by appointment through North's Property.\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Negotiator",
        "SortOrder": 10,
        "Content": "Sandra Conmy"
      }
